<section id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Data Visualization.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On ChartMimic, both of our models lead all open baselines. Specifically, <span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PrismaCoder</span>-35B outperforms most proprietary models under both settings. Notably, our 9B model demonstrates the most substantial improvement over its base (the lowest among all evaluated models) and even surpasses most proprietary models.
This clearly demonstrates the quality and utility of our data.
In addition, the low-level score evaluates rendered text, layout, chart type, and color fidelity, which means our model is more capable of generating those details.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Scientific and Vector Graphics.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On chemical-structure code, <span id="S5.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PrismaCoder</span>-35B parses
every output and reaches the highest Tanimoto similarity in the table (97.56). On
InteractScience’s visual lens both models lead the open baselines, while
image-conditioned SVG is the one vision-centric column led by an open baseline, VinciCoder-8B. Full per-benchmark metrics are presented in
Appendix <a href="#A7" title="Appendix G Full Per-Benchmark Results ‣ PrismaCoder: Pushing the Boundaries of Open Multimodal Code Intelligence through Decomposed Rubric Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">§</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">G</span></a>, and a chart-to-code case across training stages in Appendix <a href="#A9" title="Appendix I Case Studies ‣ PrismaCoder: Pushing the Boundaries of Open Multimodal Code Intelligence through Decomposed Rubric Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">§</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">I</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
