<section id="S5.SS4.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Interactive Applications and Plots.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">On ArtifactsBench, both models exceed all open baselines and <span id="S5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">GPT-4o</span> on the overall score (<a href="#S5.T3" title="In 5.4. Text-Centric Results ‣ 5. Experiments ‣ PrismaCoder: Pushing the Boundaries of Open Multimodal Code Intelligence through Decomposed Rubric Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). On InteractScience’s programmatic lens, <span id="S5.SS4.SSS0.Px1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PrismaCoder</span>-35B scores 28.00, above the best open baseline and comparable to Gemini 3 Flash. Scaling from 9B to 35B raises the InteractScience PFT score by 3.20 points.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Long-Tail Visual Languages.</h4>

<div id="S5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PrismaCoder</span>-35B leads open baselines on all three VisPlotBench metrics (<a href="#S5.T3" title="In 5.4. Text-Centric Results ‣ 5. Experiments ‣ PrismaCoder: Pushing the Boundaries of Open Multimodal Code Intelligence through Decomposed Rubric Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Tab.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>). Its Mean score is 11.02 points above their best, comparable to Claude Sonnet 4.6.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
