<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Rubric Synthesis Prompts and Examples</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Web UI reconstruction must be evaluated from two complementary perspectives: whether the generated HTML/CSS implements the required content and structure, and whether its rendered output reproduces the intended visual appearance.
A single holistic score often conflates these two aspects and provides little evidence about the source of an error.
We therefore synthesize two sets of sample-specific binary rubrics from the task instruction and reference screenshot.
Code rubrics target properties that can be verified directly from the implementation, whereas vision rubrics target properties observable in the rendered page.
<a href="#A3.F8" title="In Appendix C Rubric Synthesis Prompts and Examples ‣ PrismaCoder: Pushing the Boundaries of Open Multimodal Code Intelligence through Decomposed Rubric Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a> and <a href="#A3.F9" title="Fig. 9 ‣ Appendix C Rubric Synthesis Prompts and Examples ‣ PrismaCoder: Pushing the Boundaries of Open Multimodal Code Intelligence through Decomposed Rubric Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a> show the corresponding prompt templates.
Both prompts organize checks into shared quality criteria and sample-dependent requirements, and assign each check a weight according to its importance.
The difficulty level assigned to the instruction enters both prompts as an item budget, so harder samples receive more criteria (<a href="#S3.SS1" title="3.1. Elastic Rubric Scorer ‣ 3. PrismaForge ‣ PrismaCoder: Pushing the Boundaries of Open Multimodal Code Intelligence through Decomposed Rubric Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">§</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.1</span></a>).
The templates are abridged to remove repetitive wording.</p>
</div>
