<div id="A3.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">The complementary roles of the two rubric views are illustrated by the representative reconstruction in <a href="#S3.F3" title="In 3.1. Elastic Rubric Scorer ‣ 3. PrismaForge ‣ PrismaCoder: Pushing the Boundaries of Open Multimodal Code Intelligence through Decomposed Rubric Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.
Code rubrics verify that the expected elements and implementation constraints are present, whereas vision rubrics reveal rendering failures that may remain hidden in
otherwise valid HTML/CSS.
In this example, the synthesized page preserves the reference’s overall content, colors, and organization, yet contains a salient local layout failure.
It receives a perfect code-rubric score of <math id="A3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1.0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1.0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1.0</annotation></semantics></math>, indicating that the implementation contains the expected structure and content.
It also obtains a holistic LLM judgment score of <math id="A3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="78" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>78</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">78</annotation></semantics></math>, outperforming approximately <math id="A3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="78.6\%" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>78.6</mn><mo>%</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">78.6\%</annotation></semantics></math> of all samples.
Nevertheless, our sample-specific vision rubrics assign an aggregate score of only <math id="A3.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0.182" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0.182</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0.182</annotation></semantics></math>.
They identify that the footer is incorrectly positioned in the middle of the page, where it overlaps and clips the third service button and disrupts the intended vertical hierarchy.
They also capture that the synthesized buttons have square rather than rounded corners.
We next examine the individual judgments that produce this discrepancy.</p>
</div>
