checks behind these aggregate scores. The code evaluator passes all five
checks because the source contains the expected colors, stacking mechanism,
centering rule, footer styling, and copyright text. In contrast, the rendered
output passes only the horizontal-centering check; the remaining vision
rubrics expose the misplaced footer, clipped service button, and incorrect
button corners.</p>
