<section id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">VisPlotBench.</h4>

<div id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A7.T11" title="Tab. 11 ‣ VisPlotBench. ‣ G.1. Visualization ‣ Appendix G Full Per-Benchmark Results ‣ PrismaCoder: Pushing the Boundaries of Open Multimodal Code Intelligence through Decomposed Rubric Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> averages the three metrics over the eight languages, and
Table <a href="#A7.T12" title="Tab. 12 ‣ VisPlotBench. ‣ G.1. Visualization ‣ Appendix G Full Per-Benchmark Results ‣ PrismaCoder: Pushing the Boundaries of Open Multimodal Code Intelligence through Decomposed Rubric Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> lists the incorrect-code rate per language. <span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PrismaCoder</span>-35B has
the lowest incorrect-code rate of every model in the table (28.86%) and the highest mean and
good-plot scores under both lenses. The mean task score of
<span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PrismaCoder</span>-35B is 62.47, against 23.95 for the best VinciCoder model, and <span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PrismaCoder</span>-9B
leads both VinciCoder models on every column. Per language, the remaining failures concentrate
on LilyPond, <span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_LaTeX_logo" style="letter-spacing:-0.2em; margin-right:0.1em;">L<span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:0.4ex;font-variant:small-caps;;">a</span>T<span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.4.2" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.2ex;font-variant:small-caps;font-size:120%;">e</span>X</span>, and Asymptote, where both models still break more programs than the
specialized open baselines. On the web and diagram formats the picture reverses:
<span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.5" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PrismaCoder</span>-35B has the lowest incorrect-code rate of every model on Vega-Lite and HTML and
produces no broken program on SVG, and <span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1.1.6" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PrismaCoder</span>-9B is the strongest open model on HTML.</p>
</div>
