<p id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A7.T11" title="Tab. 11 ‣ VisPlotBench. ‣ G.1. Visualization ‣ Appendix G Full Per-Benchmark Results ‣ PrismaCoder: Pushing the Boundaries of Open Multimodal Code Intelligence through Decomposed Rubric Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> reports the image-conditioned lens (ISVGen), the text-conditioned lens
(TSVGen), and the benchmark’s final score. <span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PrismaCoder</span>-35B has the highest final score in the
table (72.96), and both of our models lead every open baseline on TSVGen. VinciCoder’s strength sits in ISVGen alone, the lens its training
targets, and its text-conditioned scores are the lowest among the open models.
<span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px4.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PrismaCoder</span>-35B comes within about three points of it on ISVGen and leads it by seven on
TSVGen, so the final score favors the balanced profile.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px5" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">ChemDraw.</h4>

<div id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#A7.T13" title="Tab. 13 ‣ ChemDraw. ‣ G.1. Visualization ‣ Appendix G Full Per-Benchmark Results ‣ PrismaCoder: Pushing the Boundaries of Open Multimodal Code Intelligence through Decomposed Rubric Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> adds exact match and two Tanimoto thresholds to the two columns of the
main table. <span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PrismaCoder</span>-35B leads every column. All 128 of its outputs parse, 92.19% match
the reference molecule exactly, and 95.31% reach a Tanimoto similarity of 1. <span id="A7.SS1.SSS0.Px5.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PrismaCoder</span>-9B is
second on every column and above every proprietary model on exact match and Tanimoto
similarity. Both are large gains over the Qwen3.5 bases, whose exact-match rates are 33.59% and
53.12%. The mean Tanimoto similarity is averaged over RDKit-valid outputs only, so the 81.39 of
Gemini 3 Flash covers the 63% of its outputs that parse, whereas ours cover every sample.</p>
</div>
