<section id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">DesignBench.</h4>

<div id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The detailed results in Table <a href="#A7.T15" title="Tab. 15 ‣ DesignBench. ‣ G.2. WebDev ‣ Appendix G Full Per-Benchmark Results ‣ PrismaCoder: Pushing the Boundaries of Open Multimodal Code Intelligence through Decomposed Rubric Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> show that the generation gains are consistent across multiple visual metrics.
<span id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PrismaCoder</span>-9B reaches a Judge score of 69.95 and a CLIP score of 84.77, while reducing MAE to 42.07 and increasing SSIM to 0.6956.
<span id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PrismaCoder</span>-35B exhibits a nearly identical profile and achieves the lowest MAE and highest SSIM among the evaluated models.
The agreement across Judge, CLIP, MAE, and SSIM indicates that the improvement is not tied to a particular evaluator, but is consistently reflected across multiple complementary measures of visual similarity.
Editing shows a more nuanced pattern: both <span id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PrismaCoder</span> models achieve an Editing-Judge score of about 8.9, substantially exceeding the prior open baselines and matching GPT-4o, while remaining slightly behind Gemini 3.1 Pro.
In contrast, their CMS and image-based similarity metrics are less competitive with the strongest proprietary models.
This difference can be partly attributed to the reference-dependent nature of these metrics.
CMS measures the overlap between the code lines modified by the model and those modified in the reference implementation, so a correct edit may still receive a lower score when it is realized through different code locations.
Similarly, MAE and SSIM compare the resulting rendering against a specific reference output and can penalize visually different but still valid implementations.
The strong Editing-Judge scores therefore suggest that <span id="A7.SS2.SSS0.Px2.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PrismaCoder</span> reliably completes the requested modifications, even when its implementation and rendering differ from the reference.</p>
</div>
