<section id="A9" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix I </span>Case Studies</h2>

<div id="A9.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A9.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Six qualitative cases drawn from VisPlotBench, one per format family. Three
compare <span id="A9.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PrismaCoder</span>-9B against its Qwen3.5-9B base (<span id="A9.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_LaTeX_logo" style="letter-spacing:-0.2em; margin-right:0.1em;">L<span id="A9.p1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:0.4ex;font-variant:small-caps;;">a</span>T<span id="A9.p1.1.2.2" class="ltx_text" style="position:relative; bottom:-0.2ex;font-variant:small-caps;font-size:120%;">e</span>X</span>, SVG, Mermaid); three
compare <span id="A9.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PrismaCoder</span>-35B against its SFT-only variant (Vega-Lite, HTML,
Python), isolating what the rubric-based RL stage adds. In every case the
middle panel executes and renders, and the failure is visual. A seventh case,
chart-to-code on ChartMimic, follows <span id="A9.p1.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">PrismaCoder</span>-9B across its training stages
(<a href="#A9.F16" title="In Appendix I Case Studies ‣ PrismaCoder: Pushing the Boundaries of Open Multimodal Code Intelligence through Decomposed Rubric Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a>) and sets the result beside an open and two
proprietary references (<a href="#A9.F17" title="In Appendix I Case Studies ‣ PrismaCoder: Pushing the Boundaries of Open Multimodal Code Intelligence through Decomposed Rubric Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Fig.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>). Four front-end cases
close the appendix, two screenshot-to-page generations from Design2Code and two
instruction-driven edits from DesignBench, each across the same training stages
(<a href="#A9.F18" title="In Appendix I Case Studies ‣ PrismaCoder: Pushing the Boundaries of Open Multimodal Code Intelligence through Decomposed Rubric Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Figs.</span> <span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>, <a href="#A9.F19" title="Fig. 19 ‣ Appendix I Case Studies ‣ PrismaCoder: Pushing the Boundaries of Open Multimodal Code Intelligence through Decomposed Rubric Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">19</span></a>, <a href="#A9.F20" title="Fig. 20 ‣ Appendix I Case Studies ‣ PrismaCoder: Pushing the Boundaries of Open Multimodal Code Intelligence through Decomposed Rubric Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">20</span></a> and <a href="#A9.F21" title="Fig. 21 ‣ Appendix I Case Studies ‣ PrismaCoder: Pushing the Boundaries of Open Multimodal Code Intelligence through Decomposed Rubric Synthesis" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>).</p>
</div>
